// The single registration manifest of the KiteFFmpeg JNI adapter (S1.c.1 step 4).
//
// Every non-comment record is:
//
//   CLASS | KOTLIN_NAME | JVM_DESCRIPTOR | C_FUNCTION
//
// CLASS is the binary name of the Kotlin bridge class declaring the private external method.
// KOTLIN_NAME is that method's exact name. JVM_DESCRIPTOR is its exact JNI descriptor.
// C_FUNCTION is the kj_* implementation registered for it. The surrounding section and function
// prefix supply its category and handle/result convention. There is deliberately no fifth field.
// The conventions are:
//
//   token(K)   returns a jlong handle of kind K, 0 meaning refused/none
//   int        returns a raw FFmpeg int (negative AVERROR travels to Kotlin uninterpreted)
//   long/bool/void/string/bytes  what they say
//
// kj_registration.c includes THIS file (through the KJ_METHOD X-macro) to build its
// JNINativeMethod tables. Internals.jvm.kt has exactly one private external per row; buildSrc's
// parser validates four fields, exact names and JVM descriptors, while an isolated-JVM control
// loads a deliberately corrupted generated manifest and requires RegisterNatives to fail. There is
// deliberately no second native-registration list.
//
// The two exception classes the adapter throws (kj_util.c) and the keep rule must name:
//   io.github.yuroyami.kiteffmpeg.JniHandleException
//   io.github.yuroyami.kiteffmpeg.JniNativeException
//
// Bridge class for every current row:
//   io/github/yuroyami/kiteffmpeg/Internals
//
// Format for the X-macro consumer: KJ_METHOD(class, name, descriptor, cfunc)

// ── abi: identity, version, VM attach (kj_abi.c) ─ COMPLETE ─────────────────────────────────
